# Build backends, locked by hash like every other dependency.
#
# pyspark 4.0.1 is published only as a source archive, so installing it builds a
# wheel. With build isolation pip would fetch these into a throwaway environment
# WITHOUT checking hashes, leaving a hole in a contract that hash-checks
# everything else. scripts/install_locked.sh installs this lock first and then
# builds with --no-build-isolation. Compiled by `make lock`.
setuptools>=69
wheel
